{"skill":{"slug":"yt-dlp-downloader-skill","displayName":"Yt Dlp Downloader"},"version":{"version":"0.1.0","createdAt":1769515135889,"changelog":"Initial release of yt-dlp-downloader-skill.\n\n- Enables video and audio downloads from YouTube, Bilibili, Twitter, TikTok, and thousands of other sites using yt-dlp.\n- Supports downloading best quality video, extracting audio as MP3, downloading subtitles, and selecting video quality.\n- Provides command examples and troubleshooting guidance for common errors (e.g., YouTube 403 errors, missing dependencies).\n- Workflow adapts commands based on user needs and source platform (e.g., always using browser cookies for YouTube).\n- Triggers on multi-language keywords such as \"下载视频\", \"download video\", \"extract audio\", \"B站\", and \"抖音\".","changelogSource":"auto","license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":6071,"sha256":"d37357ff0ac8ebe080608f2a9c6c426c17058b7a4c19fbd767f0a0b6a0a2d324","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2137,"sha256":"1b5022d54691804a3ac60505750dbe39a12f2f447010abe84dd97723fe87b42a","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789021974740,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"4aa77a4722ef4e33de7728e79d401ebfe9f065c968287bf94db7fe0b4f10cfee","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/4aa77a4722ef4e33de7728e79d401ebfe9f065c968287bf94db7fe0b4f10cfee","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: yt-dlp-downloader-skill\nVersion: 0.1.0\n\nThe skill is classified as suspicious due to two main security concerns found in `SKILL.md`. Firstly, it explicitly instructs the `yt-dlp` tool to access browser cookies via `--cookies-from-browser chrome`, which involves handling sensitive user data, even if justified for bypassing YouTube's 403 errors. Secondly, the workflow instructs the AI agent to execute commands with `required_permissions: [\"all\", \"network\"]`. The 'all' permission is overly broad for a video downloading task, granting extensive system access beyond what is strictly necessary for `yt-dlp`'s stated functionality, thereby introducing significant risk.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779160123642},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":77,"severity":"HIGH","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":7,"checkedAt":1789021974740},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"The skill does what it claims, but it routinely tells the agent to use browser cookies and broad shell permissions without enough user control or warning.","dimensions":[{"detail":"The workflow instructs execution with required_permissions [\"all\", \"network\"], which is broader than needed for a download task and increases impact if a URL, dependency, or parser is unsafe.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The skill recommends installing and upgrading yt-dlp and ffmpeg through pip and brew without pinning versions or hashes, creating mutable dependency risk but not showing malicious package use.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The workflow says YouTube downloads should always use --cookies-from-browser chrome, which accesses local browser session data even when an unauthenticated download may be sufficient.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"No persistence mechanism, background worker, scheduled task, memory modification, tool hijacking, or privilege escalation path was found in the artifact.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The stated purpose is a yt-dlp video downloader, and the commands are generally aligned with downloading videos, extracting audio, subtitles, playlists, and formats.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"note"}],"guidance":"Review this skill before installing. Use it only if you are comfortable with an agent running yt-dlp locally, writing downloads to disk, and possibly accessing browser cookies. Prefer anonymous downloads first, require explicit approval before any cookie-based command, avoid required_permissions [\"all\", \"network\"] when narrower permissions are available, and install dependencies from a trusted, pinned environment.","findings":"[YR1] unexpected: The match is explained by repeated --cookies-from-browser examples, not by an embedded credential-stealing payload; the sensitive-cookie concern remains, but the malware-signature framing is not supported by the artifact.\n[SSD-3] unexpected: The artifact does operationalize downloads with browser-cookie use and broad shell permissions; using cookies may fit some authenticated download cases, but making it routine and automatic is overbroad.\n[SQP-2] unexpected: The artifact gives no clear privacy warning or explicit consent step before accessing browser cookies or running commands that write files and use the network.\n[SDI-2] unexpected: The artifact-backed concern is valid: browser cookie access and required_permissions [\"all\", \"network\"] exceed the minimum scope for ordinary media downloads.\n[T08] expected: Installing yt-dlp and ffmpeg is expected for this skill, but the unpinned pip and brew guidance should be treated as a supply-chain risk.\n[T05] unexpected: The static scan's concern is supported: automatic browser-cookie extraction for YouTube and unrestricted local plus network permissions are high-impact relative to the stated task.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789021974740}}}}}